    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "German media from the far‑right to the left concur that irregular influxes at EU external borders – most visibly the recent Ceuta incidents – create measurable pressure on German asylum offices and therefore demand tighter EU‑wide border coordination and faster processing of applications. They also share the view that security concerns arising from certain asylum cases, such as criminal offences by recent Afghan returnees, justify stricter enforcement of deportation orders while insisting on safeguards for vulnerable migrants, especially women and children. Finally, all outlets treat migration policy as a decisive electoral issue, noting that parties across the spectrum are proposing legislative reforms or integration programmes to address both public anxiety and labour‑market demands.",
